# doi: pending — added when the Zenodo archive of the tagged release exists
# (issue #390, P2). The metadata Zenodo reads is committed as .zenodo.json;
# it needs no editing beyond the ORCID above. To mint the DOI:
#   1. Log in to Zenodo with the GitHub account and enable archiving for
#      darklordVirtual/REMORA-research (Zenodo -> GitHub -> toggle the repo).
#   2. Publish a GitHub release for the tag. Zenodo archives that tag and
#      mints both a version DOI and a concept DOI covering all versions.
#   3. Add the CONCEPT DOI here as `doi:` — it is the one that keeps
#      resolving as later versions are archived — and add the version DOI to
#      the release notes.
# Enabling archiving only affects releases created afterwards, so the toggle
# has to be set before the release is published, not after.
repository-code: "https://github.com/darklordVirtual/REMORA-research"
license: BUSL-1.1
type: software
keywords:
  - "AI governance"
  - "AI assurance"
  - "agent safety"
  - "selective prediction"
  - "conformal risk control"
